From: AzediZ <145237384+AzediZ@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:51:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 44/50] Skills: a paused skill queue survives a server restart

SetServerOnlineStatus() deleted every paused skill queue at each start and stop, so a queue paused
before a restart was gone when the pilot resumed training.  Saving a paused queue already replaces
the pilot's old one, and resuming deletes it.
---
 src/eve-server/ServiceDB.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/eve-server/ServiceDB.cpp b/src/eve-server/ServiceDB.cpp
index f80b9fe5..909269f6 100644
--- a/src/eve-server/ServiceDB.cpp
+++ b/src/eve-server/ServiceDB.cpp
@@ -197,7 +197,8 @@ void ServiceDB::SetServerOnlineStatus(bool online) {
     //this is only called on startup/shutdown.  reset all char online counts/status'
     sDatabase.RunQuery(err, "UPDATE chrCharacters SET online = 0 WHERE 1");
     sDatabase.RunQuery(err, "UPDATE account SET online = 0 WHERE 1");
-    sDatabase.RunQuery( err, "DELETE FROM chrPausedSkillQueue WHERE 1");
+    // paused skill queues are kept.  they were deleted here at every start and stop, so a queue paused before a
+    //  restart was gone when the pilot pressed apply (saving a paused queue already replaces the old one)
 }
 
 void ServiceDB::SetAccountOnlineStatus(uint32 accountID, bool online) {
